<p>This playbook is for leaders and practitioners working with OKRs in their organisations. It treats OKR adoption as a question of management philosophy rather than a question of writing templates, drawing on Deming's System of Profound Knowledge, Wodtke and Cutler, the post-2018 OKR reform tradition, and the wider sociotechnical literature.</p>

{% marpDeck "content/playbooks/okrs/overview.marp.md", "/playbooks/okrs/overview/" %}

<p>The playbook is structured in seven parts:</p>

<ol>
  <li><strong><a href="/playbooks/okrs/the-core-thesis/">The Core Thesis</a></strong> - OKRs as a management philosophy with a template attached.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/playbooks/okrs/reading-the-system/">Reading the System Through the Artefact</a></strong> - the four failure patterns as signals of what the management system believes.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/playbooks/okrs/two-functions/">The Two Functions</a></strong> - what OKRs do when they work: radiating intent and anchoring decisions.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/playbooks/okrs/interventions-as-constraints/">Interventions as Constraint Changes</a></strong> - visibility, rhythm, and safety as the three constraints that decide whether OKRs do their work.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/playbooks/okrs/profound-knowledge-lens/">The System of Profound Knowledge Lens</a></strong> - Deming's four parts applied to OKR practice. The diagnostic home base.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/playbooks/okrs/open-questions/">Open Questions</a></strong> - what is not yet settled.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/playbooks/okrs/acknowledgements/">Acknowledgements and References</a></strong>.</li>
</ol>

<p>Elements of the framework are hypotheses rather than proven positions. They are marked as such throughout.</p>

<p>The first artefact is <strong><a href="/playbooks/okrs/reading-instrument/">The Reading Instrument</a></strong> - a structured way to read your own OKR practice as evidence of what your management system actually is. Further artefacts will be added as they develop in practice.</p>
